From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:21:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Show received media inline and send voice notes and
 video

The webOS transport drops libpurple imgstore images (<img id=N>), and the
Messaging app can only show media from a URL or a local file. Teams voice
notes and video clips also need their own message formats to show up on
other Teams clients.

Received:
- Save downloaded media under /media/internal/.im-attachments/teams/,
  named by SHA-1 with an extension from the magic bytes, and put a
  file:// URL in the message instead of an imgstore image and a "Click
  here to view full version" link. Accept */* so audio comes through.
- Download audio, video and animation media cards to such a file bubble,
  and remove the empty InputExtension placeholder span so a voice note is
  not followed by a blank message.
- Convert AAC .m4a voice notes to WAV with gst-launch-0.10, since the
  legacy webOS media server cannot play AAC.
- Show OneDrive file attachments (docx, pptx, ...) as a link to their
  shareUrl or fileUrl, since objectUrl needs a browser session.

Sent:
- Voice notes: convert the recorder's audio to AAC/M4A with faac and
  ffmpeg (run with a clean environment), upload it as a "sharing/audio"
  object and send an audio card with the duration taken from the Ogg
  source.
- Video (mp4, mov, m4v, 3gp): upload as "sharing/video" and send an
  inline AMSVideo <video> element with width, height and duration read
  from the mp4 header, which is the format Teams clients send.

The paths and helper binaries are those of legacy webOS (HP TouchPad).
gst-launch-0.10 and faac are not on LuneOS, so there the conversions
fail and the original file is kept. Parts of the sending side (audio
card, AMSVideo) could go upstream once separated from the webOS file
handling.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
